---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
---
<Base title="Bandarmology" current="bandar"
  description="Broker flow on the IDX's most-traded stocks: big-ticket pressure (LPM), foreign flow, volume rotation and intensity, from the regular-market broker summary.">

  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <div class="kicker">Bandarmology · <span id="universe-count">—</span> most-traded stocks</div>
      <h1>Who's pressing on the tape</h1>
      <p class="dek">Four readings of the day's broker summary: whether the brokers trading in unusually big tickets
        leaned to the buy or the sell side, where foreign money went, how much of the volume was churn, and how
        concentrated the trading was. They describe the flow. They do not forecast it — see the method note.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="hero" aria-label="Latest reading">
      <div class="hero-lead">
        <div class="hero-label">Big-ticket pressure rising · <span id="hero-date">latest session</span></div>
        <div class="hero-figure" id="acc-count">—</div>
        <div class="hero-verdict" id="acc-verdict">Reading the broker summaries…</div>
        <dl class="hero-meta">
          <div><dt>Falling</dt><dd id="dist-count">—</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Quiet accumulation</dt><dd id="div-count">—</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="tiles">
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">LPM rising</div><div class="tile-value up" id="t-acc">—</div><div class="tile-note">20-day change ≥ 1σ</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">LPM falling</div><div class="tile-value down" id="t-dist">—</div><div class="tile-note">20-day change ≤ −1σ</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Quiet accumulation</div><div class="tile-value" id="t-div">—</div><div class="tile-note">LPM up, price not</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Foreign, 20 days</div><div class="tile-value" id="t-flow">—</div><div class="tile-note">Net, across these stocks</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Churning</div><div class="tile-value" id="t-churn">—</div><div class="tile-note">Rotation ≥ 1σ above usual</div></div>
        <div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">Odd intensity</div><div class="tile-value" id="t-int">—</div><div class="tile-note">Beyond ±2σ of its own</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="toolbar">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="toolbar-label" id="band-label">Show</span>
      <div class="segmented" id="band" role="group" aria-labelledby="band-label">
        <button type="button" data-band="all" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
        <button type="button" data-band="acc" aria-pressed="false">LPM rising</button>
        <button type="button" data-band="dist" aria-pressed="false">LPM falling</button>
        <button type="button" data-band="div" aria-pressed="false">Quiet accumulation</button>
      </div>
      <span class="spacer"></span>
      <input type="search" id="search-input" class="search" placeholder="Ticker…" aria-label="Filter by ticker">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="figure" aria-labelledby="stocks-title">
      <div class="figure-head">
        <span class="figure-no">Tab. A</span>
        <h2 id="stocks-title">The board</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="table-tools">
        <p class="figure-dek" style="margin:0">Every stock covered, strongest 20-day LPM rise first. σ readings compare a
          stock with its own history, so a small cap and BBCA rank on the same footing. Click a row for its charts.</p>
        <span class="table-count" id="row-count"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table id="data-table" class="data-table clickable-rows"></table></div>
      <div class="table-more"><button type="button" class="btn" id="row-more" hidden>Show all</button></div>
    </section>

    <section class="figure" aria-labelledby="stock-title">
      <div class="figure-head">
        <span class="figure-no">Stock</span>
        <h2 id="stock-title">—</h2>
        <div class="figure-legend">
          <label class="visually-hidden" for="stock-select">Stock</label>
          <select id="stock-select" class="search" style="min-width:8rem"></select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="figure-dek" id="stock-dek">Pick a stock from the board.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="figure-grid">
      <Figure no="Fig. I" title="Price" chart="price" size="short" dek="Daily close, rupiah." />
      <Figure no="Fig. II" title="LPM" chart="lpm" size="short"
        dek="Running total of big-ticket pressure, from zero at the start of the record. Rising = big tickets leaning to the buy side.">
        <Fragment slot="how">
          <p>Each day, a broker's buy side counts if its average ticket (lots per trade) is at least the stock's
            75th-percentile ticket of the last 200 sessions; sell sides likewise. The day adds the close times the
            difference between the counted buyers' and sellers' average ticket. Shown scale-free: Bandar Metrics
            multiplies each stock by its own fixed constant, which changes the height of the line, never its shape.</p>
        </Fragment>
      </Figure>
      <Figure no="Fig. III" title="LPM, day by day" chart="lpmday" size="short"
        dek="Each session's addition to the line. Green, big buyers outsized big sellers; red, the reverse." />
      <Figure no="Fig. IV" title="Foreign flow" chart="flow" size="short"
        dek="Running total of net foreign buying, rupiah, from the start of the record." />
      <Figure no="Fig. V" title="Volume rotation" chart="vr" size="short"
        dek="The day's volume over the net amount that changed hands between brokers. High, churn; near 1, one-way flow." />
      <Figure no="Fig. VI" title="Intensity" chart="int" size="short"
        dek="Volume over trades to the fourth, log₁₀ — few trades carrying a lot of volume read high. Compare a stock only with itself." />
    </div>

    <section class="figure" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <div class="figure-head">
        <span class="figure-no">Method</span>
        <h2 id="method-title">Terms of the reading</h2>
      </div>
      <dl class="method">
        <div><dt>Source</dt><dd>Stockbit's regular-market broker summary (gross: every broker's buy and sell side,
          with its lots and number of trades) and daily price history, fetched after the close each weekday.
          The <b>most-traded <span id="m-universe">100</span></b> stocks by median value, re-ranked monthly.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>LPM</dt><dd>Our reconstruction of Bandar Metrics' Liquidity Pressure Model, which matches its published
          values exactly once its per-stock constant is applied. Here it is shown <b>scale-free</b> (constant 1): direction and
          shape are the same, the numbers are not comparable across stocks — use the σ readings for that.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>σ readings</dt><dd>A 20-day change divided by the stock's own daily-change volatility (up to 250 sessions),
          or a level against its own history. ±1σ is unusual, ±2σ rare. New listings show none until they have
          60 sessions.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Quiet accumulation</dt><dd>LPM up at least 1σ over 20 sessions while the price is flat or down.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Not a signal</dt><dd>Tested on 170 liquid stocks over 2021–2026 (entry the session after the reading,
          after costs): LPM alone had <b>no reliable edge</b>, "quiet accumulation" was followed by
          <i>under</i>performance in 2023–24, and filtering momentum by rising LPM made it worse. Foreign flow helped only
          in 2021–22. Read this page as a description of who traded how, not as a forecast.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>
  </div>

  <style>
    :global(.clickable-rows tbody tr) { cursor: pointer; }
    :global(.clickable-rows tbody tr[aria-selected="true"]) { background: var(--paper-deep, rgba(0,0,0,.04)); }
  </style>
  <script src="../lib/bandarmology.js"></script>
</Base>
